From 7a2342fa378a8431372ce5bfe22e6882da87ecbc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 21:44:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Kernels: pattern of the tangent operator built from the
 elements

The local matrix of the tangent operator assembled by kernels is
created from the degrees of freedom of the elements
(batch::makeAssembledStiffnessMatrix), at the first call of
GetGradient: the element loop of MFEM is no longer used to build its
pattern. In each row, the diagonal entry comes first, then the other
columns, sorted: the ordering of hypre, which mfem::HypreParMatrix
imposes in place on the rows of the local matrix that it aliases
(hypre_CSRMatrixReorder), so that the rows of a sorted matrix would not
stay sorted in parallel. The kernel tests the first column of the row,
then searches the others by bisection, then linearly (any ordering is
supported).

Beam (111843 unknowns, 1 process, 10 tangent operators): 0.16 s on the
GPU instead of 1.26 s, 4.00 s on a CPU core instead of 4.47 s for the
element loop of MFEM (the linear search in the rows dominated).
